==Strategy==
This is a pretty standard Aku/Alien stage. The startoff is the biggest problem, with practically no cash and bulky GreGories ready to slam your base into next year. Send a few [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycats]] to fight the Shibaliens and spawn [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] as soon as possible. 

The Strat is to support Newtone and keep him alive while he chips down all the threats here. Knockback is particularly strong here to ward off the encroaching Le’Behemoths, so bring [[Pied Piper Cat (Rare Cat)|Brass Cat]] to snipe its shield and [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] to keep it back. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] is great as a midranger and Crowd-Control option from the frontliners, and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] does Can Can things. Once you kill the first pair of Techn-old and Le’Behemoth, you will have enough cash to snowball and push to the base, despite the second pair.

==Trivia==
*Room for Dessert's Japanese name, Betsubara no Iriguchi (別腹の入り口, "Separate Stomach Entrance"), does not refer to a literal extra stomach; 別腹 ''betsubara'' means an appetite you may have even while full, usually in the context of still wanting dessert after a meal, as though you had a "separate stomach" just for dessert.

